## System Context

The component operates as part of an AI-assisted SDV engineering and MBSE toolchain.

Natural-language automotive requirements are provided to an n8n-orchestrated multi-agent workflow. The Generator Agent combines these requirements with retrieved VSS information and previously validated architectural state to generate UML/PlantUML models.

The workflow first generates the structural Class diagram. After validation, this model becomes part of the persistent architectural state and constrains generation of the Activity diagram. The validated Class and Activity diagrams subsequently constrain generation of the Sequence diagram.

Generated models first pass deterministic syntax validation. Models that satisfy syntax requirements are subsequently analyzed by an independent AI Validator Agent for semantic and cross-view consistency.

When the Validator Agent identifies an inconsistency, the workflow triggers an iterative correction cycle. If the problem originates in an upstream architectural view, dynamic backtracking returns execution to the corresponding generation stage. The updated model is then propagated through the dependent views until the required level of architectural consistency is achieved.

The resulting validated models can be rendered as UML diagrams and provided to downstream MBSE, SDV architecture, simulation, testing, and engineering activities.

